I'd say you're doing very nicely indeed. In your position, my next
priority would be setting up a cosy little stash near a
conveniently-located altar somewhere to serve as a base of operations.
The trick to progressing from here is to play slowly. Clear a few
levels, gather goodies, bring them back to the altar for ID/ Enchant/
Use. Rinse and repeat. Obviously this slow and methodical method takes
time, patience, and lots of food, but if you've reached Soko then food
is unlikely to be a problem for a long while yet. If you can lay your
hands of a fishing pole, then it can cease to be a problem permanently.


Your AC is pretty good for the time being, I'd say, but you will want
to get that armour enchanted up. Also, start thinking about getting
some priest protection before your levels get too high- maybe pick up a
pickaxe and make a few withdrawals from the bank of Croesus. The most
conspicuous lack in your inventory imho is speed boots. That might be
the best place for a wish. I wouldn't waste a wish on a BoH in [s] for
the reason outlined below:

